rue, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 1, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 303, \"v\": 1465, \"window\": [0, 100000]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 50243, "tokens_after": 50243, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_23", "tool": "compute", "args": {"expression": "interval_len / delta", "values": {"interval_len": 38399, "delta": 600}}, "result_digest": "bc04bfce5bd6d57d", "result_summary": "{\"expression\": \"interval_len / delta\", \"result\": 63.998333333333335}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 50243, "tokens_after": 50243, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_44f03991", "decision": "insufficient", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [303, 1293, 1583, 726, 28, 1465], "window": [28296, 66695], "confidence": 0.6, "narrative": "303 never contacts 1293 directly (step_13). Untimed 2-hop routes exist (303->1583->1293, 303->726->1293) and a 3-hop route 303->1465->28->1293, but every hop is a single one-off event, and the two relays that carry the shortest paths (1583, 28) are the graph's top-2 hubs (773 and 1204 events, 540 and 746 partners, 2712 triangles for 1583), so their co-adjacency to both endpoints is the expected hub confounder rather than evidence of influence. Decisively, no available tool returns event timestamps or supports time-filtered queries: all results are aggregated over the full horizon [0,100000], so neither the ordering nor the <=600-unit inter-event gap could be checked for any hop. With a 38,399-unit query interval versus a 600-unit admissible gap (~64x slack, step_23), a static path carries little weight. Hence the temporal evidence is insufficient to affirm or deny the cascade.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_23", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings**\n\n- Structurally, 303 and 1293 are *not* directly connected (step_13), but there are 2-hop paths: 303\u21921583\u21921293 (steps 06, 07) and 303\u2192726\u21921293 (steps 18, 19), plus 303\u21921465\u219228\u21921293 (steps 22, 17, 21).\n- Each of these edges is a **single event** (n_events = 1 in each direction), so any candidate cascade rests on one specific timestamp pair per hop \u2014 extremely fragile.\n- The two shortest relays are exactly the kind of confounder the task warns about: 1583 (773 events, 540 partners, 2712 triangles) and 28 (1204 events, 746 partners) are the two most active hubs in the whole graph (steps 08, 11, 12, 14). A hub touching both endpoints is expected by chance and is not evidence of influence transfer.\n- Critically, the interval of interest spans 38,399 time units while the admissible gap is 600 \u2014 about 64 disjoint slack windows (step_23). So an untimed 2-hop path has a low prior of being time-respecting, and **none of the available tools expose event timestamps or allow time-windowed queries** (every result is reported over the full horizon [0, 100000]). I could not test ordering (t\u2081 < t\u2082) or the \u2264600 gap for a single hop.\n\n**Conclusion:** the untimed topology admits candidate paths, but the temporal evidence needed to confirm or refute a time-respecting cascade is not obtainable with the available instruments; the only paths present run through global hubs, which is the leading alternative explanation.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_44f03991\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293, 1583, 726, 28, 1465],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"303 never contacts 1293 directly (step_13). Untimed 2-hop routes exist (303->1583->1293, 303->726->1293) and a 3-hop route 303->1465->28->1293, but every hop is a single one-off event, and the two relays that carry the shortest paths (1583, 28) are the graph's top-2 hubs (773 and 1204 events, 540 and 746 partners, 2712 triangles for 1583), so their co-adjacency to both endpoints is the expected hub confounder rather than evidence of influence. Decisively, no available tool returns event timestamps or supports time-filtered queries: all results are aggregated over the full horizon [0,100000], so neither the ordering nor the <=600-unit inter-event gap could be checked for any hop. With a 38,399-unit query interval versus a 600-unit admissible gap (~64x slack, step_23), a static path carries little weight. Hence the temporal evidence is insufficient to affirm or deny the cascade.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 59061, "total_output_tokens": 7698, "total_tokens": 66759, "total_latency_ms": 112547, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}